================================================================================================================
B3 -- THE ORDERING WINDOW: dwarfs free, Milky Way nearly free, clusters retain
================================================================================================================
  criteria: dwarfs/LSBs X_RC < 0.01 ; spirals + MW X_RC < 0.1 ; clusters f_cap > 0.5
    canonical: c_ad window = (150.0, 700.0) km/s
    alt      : c_ad window = (175.0, 700.0) km/s
  [PASS] B3-1  the ordering IS achievable: a c_ad window exists on both footings, with floor set by the Milky-Way template (X_RC < 0.1) and ceiling by the clusters (f_cap > 0.5)   (canonical (150.0, 700.0), alt (175.0, 700.0) km/s)
  [PASS] B3-2  the floor sits between 130 and 250 km/s and the ceiling (clusters lose half their share) at or above 537 km/s: the collapse problem alone leaves the whole arXiv:1601.05097-allowed range above the floor open   (floor 150, ceiling 700 km/s (canonical))
  [PASS] B3-3  at the floor the dust inside 2 r_M of the most massive spirals is < 10% of M_b, so neglecting its self-gravity in Phi is consistent for the 'clean' verdicts (self-gravity can only deepen the well and INCREASE capture, so the 'captured' verdicts are conservative)   (max X_RC at floor = 0.064)

================================================================================================================
B4 -- THE BRIEF'S CRUX AS POSED: an EP-respecting fluid whose temperature rises as a^3 -- trapped or expelled?
================================================================================================================
  Milky-Way template: well depth from 2 r_M to R_max = 1.283e+05 (km/s)^2 = (358 km/s)^2
       a  c_s km/s  contrast exp(dPhi/T)  t_sound/t_H  (3/2)T/dPhi
   0.010      0.30            1.014e+304     3.82e+03     1.05e-06
   0.018      0.71            1.014e+304     6.76e+02     5.92e-06
   0.032      1.69            1.014e+304     1.20e+02     3.33e-05
   0.056      4.00            1.014e+304     2.13e+01     1.87e-04
   0.100      9.49            1.014e+304     3.78e+00     1.05e-03
   0.178     22.50            1.232e+110     6.75e-01     5.92e-03
   0.316     53.35             3.777e+19     1.23e-01     3.33e-02
   0.562    126.51             3.030e+03     2.50e-02     1.87e-01
   1.000    300.00             4.160e+00     6.72e-03     1.05e+00
  [PASS] B4-1  the equilibrium contrast collapses from >1e100 (a <= 0.1) to < 1e4 by a ~ 0.56 and < 10 by a ~ 0.9 as T rises through the well depth: the equilibrium the fluid is tracking EMPTIES the halo   (contrast(a=0.56) = 3.0e+03; contrast < 10 first at a ~ 0.94)
  [PASS] B4-2  it DOES track it where it matters: the sound-crossing time of the rotation-curve region is < 15% of the Hubble time for a >= 0.3 (c_s >= 50 km/s), i.e. throughout the epoch in which the contrast falls from 1e19 to 4 -- the evaporation is quasi-static, so early-accreted dust is EXPELLED, not trapped. (For a < 0.2 the fluid is NOT quasi-static, but there c_s is tiny and the equilibrium contrast is astronomically large: the dust is trapped only while it is still cold.)   (t_s/t_H at a = 0.32/0.56/1.0: 1.23e-01/2.50e-02/6.72e-03)
  [PASS] B4-3  energetically the same: thermal energy per unit mass (3/2)T exceeds the binding energy of the rotation-curve region once a > 0.6 for c_s(today) = 300 km/s -- the gas is unbound, not merely puffed   ((3/2)T/dPhi at a=1: 1.05)

  ...but for the ACTUAL L139 field this scenario does not arise (L153a A6): the equilibrium temperature is
  c_ad^2 = K_Q/(Qbar K_QQ), which for cosh K is the constant Z_0/Q_0 below the turnover -- the sound speed
  that 'ran as a^3' was the dynamical c_s^2 = eps c_ad^2, and its running was the running of the coupling eps.
  The dust never had a cold phase in which to fall in: with T = c_ad^2 fixed, the capture table of B2 is the
  whole story, at every epoch.
  [PASS] B4-4  for the actual field the atmosphere temperature at a = 1/1090 equals that at a = 1 to <1% (cosh, a_t = 1.27 or larger): no early cold phase, so 'trapped vs expelled' is moot   (tanh Z(rec)/tanh Z(1) = 1.1128 (a_t=1.27), 1.000686 (a_t=3))

================================================================================================================
VERDICT (B)
================================================================================================================

  With the correct temperature (c_ad^2, constant), the field-dust's fate in a halo is set by v_f^2/c_ad^2 alone
  and is EXPONENTIALLY sharp.  On the canonical footing the programme's ordering -- dwarfs free (<1% of M_b in
  the rotation-curve region), Milky-Way-class spirals nearly free (<10%), 1e14-3e14 Msun clusters retaining
  their full cosmic share -- holds for c_ad in [150, 700] km/s (alt footing (175.0, 700.0)).
  The Jeans mass grows as a^{3/2} (M_J = 3.3e+10 Msun at recombination, 1.2e+15 today at
  300 km/s): galaxy-mass dust perturbations freeze at z > 100 and only clusters keep collapsing.  The brief's crux
  (early cold accretion later pressurised) resolves as EXPELLED (quasi-static once c_s >~ 50 km/s, a >~ 0.3) for
  any fluid whose temperature rises -- and does not arise at all for this field, whose temperature never ran.
  What this lane does NOT decide: whether c_ad in that window survives the oscillatory radius (L153c), the SPARC
  double-counting with a0 refit (L153d), and the LSS growth (L153a A5-4, open).

